                <pb facs="0747" n="665" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg665"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 817.00/1656.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The American Chargé d’Affaires to the Secretary of
                        State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-07-03"><hi rendition="#italic">July 3,
                        1911</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>A vessel laden with arms left Guayaquil July 1, bound for Nicaragua, according to
                    information transmitted by the President of Salvador.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gunther.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
